Motif Paint (draw)
==================

A raster drawing application demonstrating Motif menus, tool controls, dialogs,
a DrawingArea, conditional scrollbars, and a display-independent document model.

The two-column tool panel and top action bar use original classic-style icons.
Hover over any icon for its name or keyboard shortcut. Icons are generated at
the display scale, with centered artwork and equal padding. The two-row palette
keeps its color swatches square. Ink accepts #RRGGBB.
The canvas fits the available window by default. Zoom reveals scrollbars only
when needed; resizing the window never changes the document's pixels.

Tools: Pencil, Brush, Eraser, Line, Rectangle, Ellipse, Fill, Eyedropper, Text,
and rectangular Select. Size controls brush/eraser/shape thickness. Solid shapes
fills rectangles and ellipses. Right-button drawing uses white. Copy/Cut operate
on the selection; Paste places it at the next click. This clipboard is local to
the drawing session. Text uses an X11 bitmap font. Escape cancels a gesture.

File: New, Open, Save, Save As, Quit. Images use PNG when the toolkit is built
with libpng, and uncompressed 24-bit BMP on all builds. PNG transparency is
flattened onto white. The filename extension chooses the save format. Failed
loads preserve the current document; completed saves replace the target using
a sibling temporary file. Unsaved changes and file replacement are confirmed.

Edit: sixteen undo/redo steps, including canvas size changes. Canvas size crops
or extends without resampling. The default document is 960 x 640; dimensions
must be between 1 and 4096 pixels. TrueColor X11 is required.

Keyboard: Ctrl+N/O/S, Ctrl+Shift+S, Ctrl+Z/Y, Ctrl+C/X/V, Delete, Escape,
+/- for zoom, and 0 for fit. See Help > Drawing guide in the application.

Regression checks:
  python3 tests/automated/run-paint.py --prefix /path/to/install --out "$TMPDIR/paint-check"

The runner builds the actual executable, tests the raster model with sanitizers,
and exercises the production UI through XTest on a separate Xvfb display.
